      "fact": "As of September 2015, there were no official announcements or reports indicating that Russia planned to lift the food embargo on any of the listed countries before August 6, 2016.",
      "source_date": "2015-09-01"
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Russia officially extended the food embargo on the United States, the European Union, Canada, Australia, and Norway on August 6, 2015, for a period of one year, which expires on August 5, 2016 [2]. The embargo was further expanded in June 2015 to include Iceland, Albania, Montenegro, and Liechtenstein [3]. As of the latest available information in September 2015, there was no indication or official statement from the Russian government suggesting that the embargo would be lifted prior to the expiration date of August 6, 2016 [4]. Given the explicit extension signed in August 2015 and the lack of any contrary announcements, it is highly unlikely the embargo would be lifted before the specified date.",
  "probability_yes": 0.05,
  "prediction": "no"
}

