  "reasoning": "Based on the evidence, Coachella 2020 was postponed from April to October 2020, with the new dates set for October 9-11 and 16-18 [1][2]. The official announcement on March 13, 2020, confirmed the rescheduling rather than a cancellation [2][3]. Since the question asks if the festival will be postponed or canceled before October 9, 2020, and the festival was already postponed (rescheduled) in March 2020, the event was not canceled. The rescheduling itself constitutes a postponement, which occurred before the October 9 date. Therefore, the festival was postponed, not canceled, prior to the October 9 deadline.",
  "probability_yes": 1.0,
  "prediction": "yes"
}

