    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Based on the publicly available FOMC statements from early 2021, the Federal Reserve maintained a consistent stance of continuing its asset purchase program at the established pace ($80 billion in Treasuries and $40 billion in MBS) until substantial further progress was made on employment and inflation goals [1], [2], [3]. As of the April 28, 2021 statement, there was no announcement of a reduction in monthly bond buying, nor was there an unconditional commitment to taper before the end of 2021 [4]. The statements were conditional on economic progress rather than time-based, and no specific date for a reduction had been set prior to the knowledge cutoff. Therefore, based on the information available before April 30, 2021, there is no evidence to support the claim that an announcement to reduce buying would occur before December 16, 2021.",
  "probability_yes": 0.1,
